+# Bug Assessment: Preserve orders after customer deletion and fix order pagination
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T22:10:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Support reports that deleting a customer makes their orders inaccessible through the private order detail and customer-order endpoints. The private order list also returns only its first page; later pages incorrectly have no orders and a total of zero. Orders must remain addressable by their stored customer id and snapshot data, while a later registration using the same email must be a separate account.
+
+## Symptom
+
+The customer-order endpoint rejects an id when the customer row no longer exists, despite orders retaining `customerId`. The order list's pagination/count behavior is inconsistent for later pages, and empty pages must retain matching totals. Individual order rendering must continue without a live customer and preserve billing, delivery, and placed-email data.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a customer and order, then delete the customer through `DELETE /api/v1/private/customer/{id}`.
+2. Request `GET /api/v1/private/orders/{orderId}` and `GET /api/v1/private/orders/customers/{id}`; both currently return 404.
+3. Request `GET /api/v1/private/orders?count={n}&page={p}` for a later zero-based page; the response incorrectly has no records and `recordsTotal` 0.
+4. Register a new account with the deleted customer's email and verify it does not inherit the deleted account's orders. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact integration fixture/database configuration]
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java:112-151` — customer-order listing first requires `customerService.getById`, so deleted customers cannot be queried.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:923-970` — customer-order criteria is built from the customer object instead of the persisted order customer id, and empty results are handled without preserving totals.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:936-970,1064-1094` — order list conversion has separate empty-result behavior and routes through legacy/non-legacy pagination paths.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java:138-255` — filtered order query, count query, ordering, and page calculation; the fetch-join query and count/pagination handling are the likely source of later-page/total inconsistencies.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java:17-39` — applies zero-based pagination and computes total pages; the arithmetic uses `count/pageSize + 1` rather than ceiling division.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:1107-1150` — order detail already looks up the customer opportunistically and can leave `ReadableOrder.customer` null, while populating persisted order snapshot fields.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The customer endpoint treats the customer table as the source of truth even though `Order.customerId` is a scalar historical reference, so deletion turns a valid order query into a 404. The private list uses a separate repository path whose count/pagination handling is fragile (including incorrect page-count arithmetic and a fetch-join collection query), and the facade returns an empty response before copying the database total. The order detail path is already designed to tolerate a missing customer; preserving its scalar order data and avoiding customer reattachment should satisfy the deleted-account behavior.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Make customer-order listing query orders directly by the supplied customer id, without requiring a live `Customer`; populate the response customer only when the account still exists. Ensure all private order list responses copy the query total even when the requested page is empty. Use a stable order query/count query with properly grouped filter predicates, apply zero-based page offsets, and calculate pages as ceiling(total/page size), while retaining descending newest-first ordering. Keep `Order.customerId` and `customerEmailAddress` as historical order data so deleting/re-registering accounts remains independent.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java`
+- relevant order API/repository tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Verify an order remains readable with a null customer after its customer row is deleted, including billing/delivery/email, status/history, and transactions.
+- Verify customer-id order lookup works for deleted and existing ids, is newest-first, returns the matching total, and returns zero totals for an unknown id.
+- Verify private filtered order pages are zero-based, newest-first, preserve totals on out-of-range pages, and report correct total pages.
+- Verify registering the deleted email creates an independent customer with no historical orders.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Fetch joins over collection-valued associations can duplicate rows or interact poorly with database-level pagination; the result query must avoid changing order cardinality.
+- Existing clients may depend on response fields such as `totalPages`; the correction should preserve the field while fixing its value.
+- No schema migration should be needed because orders already store scalar customer id and email snapshots; deleting a customer must not cascade-delete orders.
+- Integration tests may require the configured database and merchant fixtures.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact integration fixture/database configuration]
