+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T22:09:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Private customer-order lookup now queries the persisted order customer id even when the customer account has been deleted, while attaching customer details only for a live account. Order list pagination now preserves totals on empty pages, uses correct page-count arithmetic, and groups alternative name/phone filters correctly.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` | modified | Customer order lookup no longer returns 404 for a missing customer; it queries by historical customer id. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Empty result pages retain `recordsTotal`, `totalPages`, and an empty orders list. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java` | modified | Added customer-id filtering and grouped OR predicates in the current private order query. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java` | modified | Corrected zero-based page total calculation to ceiling division. |
+| `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/common/EntityList.java` | modified | Exposes zero pages for zero matching records instead of forcing one page. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No dedicated regression test was added; the existing integration tests require an unavailable Spring/database test context and were skipped by the test runner.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `git diff --check` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed; all six reactor modules compiled.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -Dtest=OrderTest,OrderApiIntegrationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → build passed, but the selected tests were skipped due to missing test context/configuration.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment proposed adding integration tests; no source tests were added because the available test classes are environment-dependent and skipped in this checkout. The implementation stayed within the proposed source-file scope.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add a configured API integration fixture covering customer deletion, historical order lookup, pagination, and email re-registration.
